{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/829685-what-are-your-favorite-house-rules-for-crossovers","id":829685,"title":"What are your favorite House rules for crossovers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-14T06:08:32-08:00","id":829685,"title":"What are your favorite House rules for crossovers?","content":"Self explanatory title. We all know that in a cwod crossover, while possible and other splats are referenced in the story, are severely unbalanced as incompatible rules and themes get lost in translation.<br /> <br /> So how have you all personally dealt with the strange circumstances, competing themes, drastically imbalanced parties and player attempts at mix and match templates. What are your favorite tweaks, house rules, and settings for crossovers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T12:16:51-08:00","id":829831,"title":"","content":"Frenzied Garous can be blinded by inquisitiors with True Faith (Numen).<br /> <br /> Where there are supernatural creatures near a mage and they are the first to create XFs.. then the mage is allowed to some &quot;vulgar magic&quot; like coincidental, temporally. <br /> <br /> Mages with mind sphere can break ghoul's vinculum. This can be dangerous for vampire because he can be betrayed in the worst time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T22:21:33-08:00","id":830049,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I\u2019ve mentioned these in other threads, so some of these bits may sound [annoyingly] familiar to forumites. For crossovers with the Big Three (and Wraith), in no particular order:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mages</span><br /> Consensus, paradigms, vulgar magick, etc., are central to MtA, but became convoluted when dealing with other PC splats. I use variants of DA:M rules (Pillars and Foundations) when running crossover\u2019d Mages.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Werewolves</span><br /> Mechanically, they play well with others\u2026except for Crinos. Crossover\u2019d Garou can only be in Crinos for [Rage] turns per scene.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Vampires</span><br /> Again, like Werewolves, their mechanics aren\u2019t too bad. However, sunlight is a pain in the narrative. Vampires take bashing damage from Sunlight and can soak with just Stamina. It might not kill them, but going in direct sunlight still causes some smoking, which could be a Masquerade breach. Thick clothing or at least indoors, they can still contribute to the story without having to sleep as with RAW.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Wraiths</span><br /> Risen work well for an easy answer. If a player really wants to play a Wraith, I increase (a lot!) the duration of Embody. As long the player is fine with a heavy Embody-dump, it works out.<br /> <br /> [I used an NPC Mage that bartered for wraithly service by giving rings that granted an extended Embody-like power. Yes, Wraiths\u2026that wore Rings. Wonder where I got the inspiration for that one? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ]<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Others</span><br /> I tried adapting CtD for crossovers in a Steampunk-Weird West crossover game. Everyone had fun, but I had so many ad hoc rulings that consistency became a huge issue for me. Luckily, the player was gracious and forgiving. I don\u2019t have much experience with the other lines.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T00:15:22-08:00","id":830071,"title":"","content":"I use the rule from <i>Buried Secrets</i> that any splat that uses a trait for an opposed roll that another splat doesn't have defaults to Willpower. So, Werewolves don't have Humanity, they use Willpower instead, for example. <br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T05:37:49-08:00","id":830172,"title":"","content":"Picking which ruleset is being used is a usually a good start, since combat and feat difficulties are different between every single book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T13:17:18-08:00","id":831245,"title":"","content":"For crossovers, I generally allow vampires to soak aggravated damage with Stamina, if not a more radical change to damage. It allows them to be less fragile against the kinds of things that werewolves or mages might deal with. I also let the vampire players have a ghoul character that they can play during the day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T12:48:20-08:00","id":833450,"title":"","content":"-vitae, quintessence, gnosis, glamour, sekhem etc... all equivalent, and simply different names for the same thing<br /> -ditto for banality &amp; paradox.<br /> -give all players a humanity score, and make rage the inverse of that.<br /> -penumbra, dreaming and skinlands also all the same thing, just from different perspectives.<br /> -remove all &quot;paths of doing what I feel like&quot;<br /> -replace all vampiric thaumaturgy, necromancy etc... with hedge magic, but allow the use of vitae like mana/quintessence<br /> -eliminate damage rolls, all damage values = 2/3 of what the dicepool would have been<br /> -ST plays simplified versions of shadows<br /> -eliminate trait bonus stacking: if one effect gives +2 str and another gives +1 str, the character only gets +2 str, not +3<br /> <br /> That's all I can think of at the moment, I'm sure there's more...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1815-joeduncan","name":"JoeDuncan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T14:28:41-08:00","id":833524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JoeDuncan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/829685-what-are-your-favorite-house-rules-for-crossovers?p=833450#post833450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-vitae, quintessence, gnosis, glamour, sekhem etc... all equivalent, and simply different names for the same thing<br /> -ditto for banality &amp; paradox.<br /> -give all players a humanity score, and make rage the inverse of that.<br /> -penumbra, dreaming and skinlands also all the same thing, just from different perspectives.<br /> -remove all &quot;paths of doing what I feel like&quot;<br /> -replace all vampiric thaumaturgy, necromancy etc... with hedge magic, but allow the use of vitae like mana/quintessence<br /> -eliminate damage rolls, all damage values = 2/3 of what the dicepool would have been<br /> -ST plays simplified versions of shadows<br /> -eliminate trait bonus stacking: if one effect gives +2 str and another gives +1 str, the character only gets +2 str, not +3<br /> <br /> That's all I can think of at the moment, I'm sure there's more...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> How does a mage or a changeling deal with rage? they don't seem much like berserkers to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T14:57:53-08:00","id":833540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeeDee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/829685-what-are-your-favorite-house-rules-for-crossovers?p=833524#post833524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does a mage or a changeling deal with rage? they don't seem much like berserkers to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't. Why would they?<br /> <br /> All I meant was that when something calls for a &quot;rage&quot; value for a werewolf, I use a value of &quot;10 - humanity&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1815-joeduncan","name":"JoeDuncan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T18:23:11-08:00","id":833629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JoeDuncan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/829685-what-are-your-favorite-house-rules-for-crossovers?p=833540#post833540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They don't. Why would they?<br /> <br /> All I meant was that when something calls for a &amp;quot;rage&amp;quot; value for a werewolf, I use a value of &amp;quot;10 - humanity&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems problematic for a few reasons, one being there is no reason that rage should be opposite of humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T19:22:10-08:00","id":833658,"title":"","content":"I don't allow cross overs or make the players use the example guide lines of that splat out of the back of the main book for the game I'm running.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T12:06:24-07:00","id":957763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/829685-what-are-your-favorite-house-rules-for-crossovers?p=833629#post833629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... there is no reason that rage should be opposite of humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean other than the amount of permanent Rage and level of Humanity BOTH indicating how &quot;close&quot; to the &quot;BEAST&quot; characters are?<br /> <br /> It's a simplification I use to avoid the &quot;multiplication of character stats&quot; in crossover campaigns. Works fine for me, but feel free NOT to use it if you like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1815-joeduncan","name":"JoeDuncan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T13:02:09-07:00","id":957789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JoeDuncan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/829685-what-are-your-favorite-house-rules-for-crossovers?p=957763#post957763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean other than the amount of permanent Rage and level of Humanity BOTH indicating how &quot;close&quot; to the &quot;BEAST&quot; characters are?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what Rage is though. Arguably, Primal Urge is closer to what you're referencing.<br /> But yea, the system isn't at all crossover friendly, so make up whatever rules you need to make up to facilitate it. The books are next to useless on the issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}